3. Pichai's agentic-search remarks + 12-month planning.\n4. Whitespark's Local Search Ranking Factors (proximity/categories/reviews as top factors).\n5. Secondary categories: does adding categories help, or does it dilute? Community consensus (Mike Blumenthal, Sterling Sky Davis) has found that categories do matter, but the primary category matters most. Adding secondary categories is generally not harmful.\n\nLet's try to fetch these via jina reader with actual known URLs.\n", "reasoning_details": null, "codex_reasoning_items": null, "codex_message_items": null, "platform_message_id": null, "observed": 0, "active": 1, "compacted": 0}, {"id": 491, "session_id": "20260825_100001_62bb70", "role": "tool", "content": "{\"output\": \"=== 1) WHITESPARK FACTORS ===\\nsearch, & news \\n######  Podcast \\nThe Whitespark Local Update \\n######  Local SEO email course \\nBecome a local SEO pro, for free! \\n######  Local Search Ranking Factors \\n######  Local Search Ecosystem \\n######  Guide to GBP optimization \\n######  Top Local Citation Sources by Country \\n  * Sign in \\nSign in\\n#  Local Search Ranking Factors \\n#  Your ultimate guide to local search success in 2026! \\nBy Darren Shaw \\n| \\nPublished November 6, 2025 \\nPlain-text version of this study (llms.txt)\\nIntroduction & analysisLocal pack/Maps factorsLocal organic factorsAI search visibility factorsLSA factorsConversion factorsLocal SEO mythsNegative ranking factorsSuspension risk factorsExpert contributorsExpert Q&A\\n#  Introduction & analysis \\n🔗 Copy a link to this section\\n###### Ask Darren anything about the 2026 Local Ranking Factors\\nVisit the reddit AMA to ask your burning local SEO questions and join the dialog!\\nIt has been just over 2 years since I published the last Local Search Ranking Factors report. Since then, the SEO industry has experienced significant shifts in our understanding and approach to SEO, driven by the growth of large language models (LLMs) like ChatGPT and Gemini for informational queries. \\nLocal search has remained somewhat insulated from this AI upheaval. While informational content-based websites have seen their traffic fall off a cliff with the introduction of AI Overviews, AI Mode, ChatGPT, Gemini, and others, research and discovery of local businesses is still predominantly done through Google’s local results because it’s a much better experience for local intent queries than LLM responses. \\nUnderstanding what drives local rankings and how to improve them remains incredibly valuable for businesses and agencies alike. \\nThis is not to say there haven’t been changes in local search, though. There have been significant changes. Read on to learn what’s new. \\n##  Video summary \\nWatch this video for Darren’s top highlig\", \"exit_code\": 0, \"error\": null}", "tool_call_id": "call_11034972c3dc4a50a96bc27f", "tool_calls": null, "tool_name": "terminal", "effect_disposition": null, "timestamp": 1787628639.0581732, "token_count": null, "finish_reason": null, "reasoning": null, "reasoning_content": null, "reasoning_details": null, "codex_reasoning_items": null, "codex_message_items": null, "platform_message_id": null, "observed": 0, "active": 1, "compacted": 0}, {"id": 492, "session_id": "20260825_100001_62bb70", "role": "assistant", "content": "Excellent — the 2026 Whitespark study (published November 2025) has a plain-text llms.txt version. Let me grab that — it's the most authoritative fact-check source available, and it now includes an AI-search visibility section.", "tool_call_id": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_fe6721f36b344973a9eb2cfe", "call_id": "call_fe6721f36b344973a9eb2cfe", "response_item_id": "fc_fe6721f36b344973a9eb2cfe", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "terminal", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd /tmp && curl -sL --max-time 60 -A \\\"Mozilla/5.0\\\" \\\"https://www.whitespark.ca/local-search-ranking-factors/llms.txt\\\" -o whitespark.txt -w \\\"HTTP %{http_code} size %{size_download}\\\\n\\\"; head