codex_message_items": null, "platform_message_id": null, "observed": 0, "active": 1, "compacted": 0}, {"id": 506, "session_id": "20260825_100001_62bb70", "role": "tool", "content": "{\"content\": \"1|# 006 — Site Bot Onboarding: Decision-Set & Autofill Audit\\n2|\\n3|- Task: 2026-08-24_006 (read-only research; report is the only artifact)\\n4|- Scope: `src/app/(app)/site-bot/start/page.tsx` (the full onboarding chat), `src/app/api/site-bot/generate/route.ts` (field consumption), `src/lib/gbp/*` + `src/app/api/gbp/*` + `src/app/api/gmb/pull/route.ts` (GBP data availability)\\n5|- Hebrew-safety: all Hebrew UI strings are referenced by `file:line` only; zero Hebrew bytes in this report.\\n6|- Escalation: None — read-only analysis.\\n7|\\n8|---\\n9|\\n10|## 1. Flow architecture (what the onboarding actually is)\\n11|\\n12|The entire Site Bot onboarding is a single self-contained client component:\\n13|`src/app/(app)/site-bot/start/page.tsx`. There are no sub-step components — the\\n14|`STEPS` array defined inline at `start/page.tsx:66-165` is the complete decision\\n15|set. Mechanics:\\n16|\\n17|- One question per screen; single shared text input (`start/page.tsx:331-346`).\\n18|- Sequential advance with skip support: `start/page.tsx:225-226` (steps whose\\n19|  `skip()` returns true are bypassed).\\n20|- Anti-generic one-shot probes: if a step defines `detectGeneric` and the answer\\n21|  looks generic, one follow-up probe fires, at most once per field\\n22|  (`start/page.tsx:210-217`; combine logic `start/page.tsx:219`). Probes are\\n23|  re-asks of the SAME decision, not new decisions.\\n24|- Progress bar counts visible steps (`start/page.tsx:243-245, 264`).\\n25|- On completion the collected object POSTs to `/api/site-bot/checkout/init`\\n26|  (`start/page.tsx:185-200`), which requires only `businessNiche`\\n27|  (`checkout/init/route.ts:21-23`), persists the data\\n28|  (`checkout/init/route.ts:26-31`) and opens the payment session\\n29|  (`checkout/init/route.ts:34-40`). Payment card fields live on the pay page\\n30|  (`src/app/(product)/site-bot/pay/[sessionId]/page.tsx:52-55`) — post-chat\\n31|  billing, not onboarding decisions.\\n32|- Generation consumes the persisted object in\\n33|  `src/app/api/site-bot/generate/route.ts`: hard requirement is `businessNiche`\\n34|  only (`generate/route.ts:120-122`); everything else is optional.\\n35|\\n36|Note: the marketing FAQ claims the owner answers \\\"15 questions\\\"\\n37|(`src/app/(app)/site-bot/page.tsx:37`), but the actual `STEPS` count is 14.\\n38|\\n39|## 2. Decision-set catalog (in rendered order)\\n40|\\n41|All steps in `src/app/(app)/site-bot/start/page.tsx`. \\\"Sets\\\" = `CollectedData`\\n42|fields written by the step's `apply` (schema: `src/lib/bot/prompts.ts:6-92`).\\n43|\\n44|| # | key | step def | question line | Sets | Conditional / probe notes |\\n45||---|-----|----------|---------------|------|---------------------------|\\n46|| 1 | businessName | :67-71 | :69 | businessName | — |\\n47|| 2 | businessNiche | :72-76 | :74 | businessNiche, primaryService | — |\\n48|| 3 | serviceModel | :77-89 | :79 | serviceModel | free text → enum via regex classifier :80-88 |\\n49|| 4 | streetAddress | :90-95 | :92 | streetAddress | SKIPPED unless serviceModel is location/mixed (:93) |\\n50|| 5 | targetLocation | :96-100 | :98 | targetLocation, specificCities | — |\\n51|| 6 | ownerName | :101-105 | :103 | ownerName | — |\\n52|| 7 | usp | :106-114 | :108 | usp | anti-generic probe :110-113 |\\n53|| 8 | idealClientFear | :115-123 | :117 | idealClientFear | anti-generic probe :119-122 |\\n54|| 9 | yearsAndGuarantee | :124-128 | :126 | yearsInField, guarantee | one question, two fields |\\n55|| 10 | services | :129-133 | :131 | secondaryServices | — |\\n56|| 11 | reviewQuote | :134-146 | :136 | reviewQuote, starRating (parsed :139-140) | honest \\\"none\\\" path skips field (:138); probe :142-145 |\\n57|| 12 | contact | :147-154 | :149 | contactMethod, phone, whatsappNumber (:150-153) | one question, three fields |\\n58|| 13 | businessHours | :155-159 | :157 | businessHours | \\\"no fixed hours\\\" answer skips field (:158) |\\n59|| 14 | preferredSlug | :160-164 | :162 | preferredSlug | built-in skip word drops the field (:163) |\\n60|\\n61|**Total: 14 questions.** Step 4 is skipped for field/remote service models, so\\n62|an owner sees 13 or 14 screens; up to 3 one-shot probes (steps 7, 8, 11) can add\\n63|a follow-up without adding a decision.\\n64|\\n65|### Consumed-but-never-asked fields (not onboarding decisions)\\n66|\\n67|`buildLpCopyPrompt` interpolates several `CollectedData` fields the Site Bot\\n68|chat never collects: license (`src/lib/lp/lpCopyPrompt.ts:175`), faqQuestions\\n69|(:177), urgencyLevel (:178), responseTime (:179), revenueModel (:180),\\n70|pricingNotes (:181), exclusions (:182), capacityUnit (:185). These arrive only\\n71|from the Ads Bot onboarding path; in Site Bot they render empty/default\\n72|(e.g. `generate/route.ts:103`). vatStatus and license were deliberately dropped\\n73|from the paid path (`start/page.tsx:12-13`); vatStatus is merely timestamped if\\n74|present (`generate/route.ts:194-196`). None of these count toward the decision\\n75|set.\\n76|\\n77|## 3. Classification per input\\n78|\\n79|Classes per spec: (a) auto-fillable from a GBP/Places lookup keyed on business\\n80|name + phone; (b) safe smart-default the owner can edit later; (c) genuinely\\n81|must-ask.\\n82|\\n83|| # | key | Class | One-line reason |\\n84||---|-----|-------|-----------------|\\n85|| 1 | businessName | (a) | Doubles as the lookup key — owner types it once to find the profile, then confirms the canonical name from the matched listing instead of composing it. |\\n86|| 2 | businessNiche | (a) | GBP `categories` is already in the location read mask (`src/lib/gbp/client.ts:89`) — map category to niche, owner confirms. |\\n87|| 3 | serviceModel | (b) | Inferable from the GBP category (plumber→field, clinic→location); a regex classifier already exists (`start/page.tsx:80-88`) — default it, let the owner correct. |\\n88|| 4 | streetAddress | (a) | GBP `storefrontAddress` is already in the read mask (`client.ts:89`); feeds LocalBusiness schema (`src/lib/lp/renderSitePages.ts:131-134`). |\\n89|| 5 | targetLocation | (b) | GBP gives the home-base city from the address, but the full service-area city list is owner knowledge — default from address city, owner edits; feeds core-30 cities (`src/lib/lp/coreThirty.ts:94`). |\\n90|| 6 | ownerName | (c) | The owner's personal first name is not in GBP location data; the about blurb is built on it (`lpCopyPrompt.ts:51, 144`). One word, but irreducible. |\\n91|| 7 | usp | (c) | Differentiation exists only in the owner's head; the anti-generic probe machinery (`start/page.tsx:45-50, 110-113`) exists precisely because this cannot be templated or looked up. |\\n92|| 8 | idealClientFear | (c) | Customer-psychology insight; a lookup or per-niche default would manufacture exactly the generic copy the probe system fights (`start/page.tsx:52-57`). |\\n93|| 9 | yearsAndGuarantee | (c) | Tenure and guarantee terms are the owner's own facts/promises; GBP carries neither reliably. |\\n94|| 10 | services | (b) | Seed the list from GBP categories + confirmed niche; owner edits. Core-30 requires an explicit service list (`coreThirty.ts:88-92`), so a confirmed default is enough. |\\n95|| 11 | reviewQuote | (a) | `listReviews` already fetches review text + star ratings (`client.ts:93-95`) — surface the best real review, owner picks/confirms; keeps the honest \\\"none\\\" exit. |\\n96|| 12 | contact | (a) | The number comes from GBP `phoneNumbers` (`client.ts:89`); the channel preference (phone/WhatsApp/both) is a trivial sub-decision safely defaulted to \\\"both\\\" (`start/page.tsx:150-153` already writes both fields from one number). |\\n97|| 13 | businessHours | (a)* | The GBP Business Information API exposes `regularHours`, but the current read mask (`client.ts:89`) omits it — same `getLocation` call, mask needs one added field. |\\n98|| 14 | preferredSlug | (b) | Already optional today: skip word (`start/page.tsx:163`) and deterministic slug generation both exist (`generate/route.ts:59-70, 124-127`). Pure default, zero decisions. |\\n99|\\n100|## 4. GBP data availability — what we can pull TODAY vs. new work\\n101|\\n102|### Already available behind the existing integration\\n103|\\n104|All gated by `isGbpLive()` = credentials AND `GBP_INTEGRATION_ENABLED=true`\\n105|(`client.ts:35-52`):\\n106|\\n107|- `getLocation` (`client.ts:88-91`) read mask at `client.ts:89` returns:\\n108|  `name, title, phoneNumbers, storefrontAddress, categories, websiteUri`.\\n109|  Covers: businessName, businessNiche (via categories), streetAddress,\\n110|  contact phone. `websiteUri` is available but has no corresponding Site Bot\\n111|  input today.\\n112|- `listReviews` (`client.ts:93-95`) returns review text and star ratings.\\n113|  Covers: reviewQuote + starRating.\\n114|- `listAccounts` (`client.ts:84-86`) exists for account enumeration.\\n115|\\n116|### Requires new work\\n117|\\n118|- **businessHours**: add `regularHours` (optionally `specialHours`) to the read\\n119|  mask at `client.ts:89` — no new endpoint, one-line mask change.\\n120|- **photos**: no media API is wrapped anywhere; the client wraps only Account\\n121|  Management, Business Information, and legacy v4 reviews/posts\\n122|  (`client.ts:19-24`). Photos need a new media endpoint or the Places API.\\n123|- **Account/location resolution for self-serve prospects**: today GBP ids come\\n124|  from `client.json` per existing client (`src/app/api/gbp/review-reply/route.ts:60`);\\n125|  the pull route explicitly flags that accountId resolution is not built\\n126|  (`src/app/api/gmb/pull/route.ts:60-64`). A prospect walking into Site Bot has\\n127|  no `gbpAccountId`/`gbpLocationId` on file — a claim/verify + account-match\\n128|  step would be required to use this path.\\n129|- **Unclaimed-profile lookup (the big gap)**: there is NO Places API\\n130|  integration in the repo (zero matches for `places.googleapis`, `PLACES_API`,\\n131|  `placesApi` across `src/`). The current GBP path only works for owners whose\\n132|  listing is already claimed/verified AND OAuth-connected to WAO. A public\\n133|  Places lookup keyed on name + phone (working for any publicly listed\\n134|  business, no OAuth, no claim required) would be a brand-new integration —\\n135|  and it is the only variant that serves the typical unverified Site Bot\\n136|  prospect without a Google OAuth detour mid-onboarding.\\n137|\\n138|## 5. Decision-reduction summary\\n139|\\n140|- **Current inputs: 14** sequential questions (13 rendered for field/remote\\n141|  owners; +up to 3 one-shot anti-generic probes, which are re-asks, not new\\n142|  decisions).\\n143|- **Class (a) auto-fillable: 6** — businessName, businessNiche, streetAddress,\\n144|  reviewQuote, contact, businessHours (last one pending the read-mask addition,\\n145|  `client.ts:89`).\\n146|- **Class (b) smart-defaultable: 4** — serviceModel, targetLocation, services,\\n147|  preferredSlug.\\n148|- **Class (c) must-ask: 4** — ownerName, usp, idealClientFear,\\n149|  yearsAndGuarantee.\\n150|- **Irreducible decision count: 4.** If every class-(a) field is auto-filled\\n151|  (owner confirms a pre-populated card) and every class-(b) field ships as an\\n152|  editable default, the onboarding floor is four owner-composed answers — the\\n153|  differentiation/psychology facts no lookup can supply — plus the lookup keys\\n154|  (business name, phone) which double as the answers themselves and therefore\\n155|  add no net-new decisions.\\n156|- **Headline reduction: 14 → 4 composed decisions (~71% fewer decisions);**\\n157|  the other 10 become confirm/adjust interactions on prefilled data.\\n158|\\n159|### Caveats on the floor\\n160|\\n161|1. The (a) class via the CURRENT GBP integration presupposes a claimed,\\n162|   verified, OAuth-connected profile; for unclaimed prospects only a new\\n163|   Places-API lookup (not yet in the codebase) delivers the same autofill.\\n164|2. businessHours autofill needs the `regularHours` read-mask addition\\n165|   (`client.ts:89`) — trivial, but not in place today.\\n166|3. The anti-generic probes on usp/idealClientFear/reviewQuote\\n167|   (`start/page.tsx:210-217`) must survive any autofill redesign — they are the\\n168|   guard against the generic-first-site failure mode and apply to the\\n169|   irreducible four exactly.\\n170|\\n171|---\\n172|\\n173|Verification gate: read-only task — `npm run build` N/A, `npm run test` N/A.\\n174|`git status --porcelain` shows exactly one new untracked file (this report).\\n175|\", \"total_lines\": 174, \"file_size\": 11626, \"truncated\": false, \"is_binary\": false, \"is_image\": false}", "tool_call_id": "call_2e0209501a50410687c98830", "tool_calls": null, "tool_name": "read_file", "effect_disposition": null, "timestamp": 1787629668.4308443, "token_count": null, "finish_reason": null, "reasoning": null, "reasoning_content": null, "reasoning_details": null, "codex_reasoning_items": null, "codex_message_items": null, "platform_message_id": null, "observed": 0, "active": 1, "compacted": 0}, {"id": 507, "session_id": "20260825_100001_62bb70", "role": "assistant", "content": "Good question — let me check exactly what we already have before deciding, because \"Core-30\" does ring a bell in this codebase.", "tool_call_id": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_62efbacb3cab4e63835ed3c3", "call_id": "call_62efbacb3cab4e63835ed3c3", "response_item_id": "fc_62efbacb3cab4e63835ed3c3", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "execute_code", "arguments": "{\"code\": \"from hermes_tools import terminal, search_files\\n\\n# What does coreThirty.ts actually do?\\nr = terminal(\\\"wc -l /home/eitanya/wao/src/lib/lp/coreThirty.ts; head -120 /home/eitanya/wao/src/lib/lp/coreThirty.ts\\\")\\nprint(r['output'][:3500])\\n\"}"}}, {"id": "ca