rchive/          <- Old completed tasks (cleanup weekly)\\n27|\\n28|---\\n29|\\n30|## File Naming Convention\\n31|\\n32|Every handoff file MUST follow this pattern:\\n33|\\n34|    [YYYY-MM-DD]_[SEQUENCE]_[AGENT-TARGET]_[TASK-SLUG].md\\n35|\\n36|Examples:\\n37|\\n38|    2026-08-10_001_waoengineer_fix-bot-route-rtl.md\\n39|    2026-08-10_002_waocopy_rewrite-onboarding-hebrew.md\\n40|    2026-08-10_003_waostrategy_google-ads-campaign-spec.md\\n41|\\n42|Rules:\\n43|- Date: today's date (YYYY-MM-DD)\\n44|- Sequence: 3-digit counter, reset daily (001, 002, 003...)\\n45|- Agent Target: one of waoengineer, waocopy, waoverifier-app, waoverifier-media\\n46|- Task Slug: kebab-case, max 5 words\\n47|\\n48|---\\n49|\\n50|## Execution Mode Switch\\n51|\\n52|`/handoff/EXECUTION_MODE` is a one-line file: either `hermes` or `claude-subagents`. It is the\\n53|on/off switch for which engine actually runs pending tasks, and it is binding — check it before\\n54|dispatching, don't guess or default from memory.\\n55|\\n56|Before dispatching any pending file that does NOT already declare its own execution mode in an\\n57|explicit banner at the top (see next paragraph), read `/handoff/EXECUTION_MODE` and dispatch\\n58|accordingly:\\n59|- **`hermes`** → Bash-dispatch `hermes -z ...` against the Hermes profile named in the file's\\n60|  `Target Agent` field (`waoengineer`, `waocopy`, `waoverifier-app`, `waoverifier-media`), per\\n61|  AGENTS.md's model configs.\\n62|- **`claude-subagents`** → call the matching Claude subagent via the Agent tool (`nextjs-engineer`,\\n63|  `copywriter`, `language-qa`, `seo-strategist`, `ppc-strategist`, `ux`, `verifier`,\\n64|  `instructional-designer`, etc.), using any model override the task file specifies, else the\\n65|  subagent's own charter default.\\n66|\\n67|A task file may override the global switch for itself with an explicit `⚠️ EXECUTION MODE:` banner\\n68|at the top (see `2026-08-20_001_copywriter_blue-ocean-sabra-pass.md` for the pattern) — an explicit\\n69|per-task banner always wins over the global file. Use this when a task must run a specific way\\n70|regardless of whatever the switch is set to when it's eventually picked up.\\n71|\\n72|In `claude-subagents` mode, there is no autonomous watcher process — the picking-up session itself\\n73|must read the pending file, invoke the subagent, append the completion report, and move the file to\\n74|`/completed/` or `/failed/`. In `hermes` mode, the orchestrating session performs the dispatch\\n75|itself: either `hermes kanban create` against the named profile's board (current pattern,\\n76|2026-08-24 onward) or a direct one-shot `hermes -z` Bash dispatch — the orchestrator executes the\\n77|dispatch directly, it is never handed off as a script for the user to run.\\n78|\\n79|---\\n80|\\n81|## Execution Order\\n82|\\n83|Hermes processes /pending/ files in ascending filename order, ONE task at a time.\\n84|- Never start a task whose Dependencies (see template) are not already in /completed/.\\n85|- If a dependency sits in /failed/, move the dependent task to /failed/ too, with\\n86|  a note naming the blocking task — do not attempt it.\\n87|- Parallel execution is allowed ONLY for tasks with no dependency relationship\\n88|  and different Target Agents.\\n89|\\n90|---\\n91|\\n92|## File Structure Template\\n93|\\n94|Every handoff file MUST contain ALL of these sections.\\n95|Missing sections = Hermes rejects the file.\\n96|\\n97|    # [TASK TITLE]\\n98|\\n99|    ⚠️ HEBREW-SAFETY: waoengineer types ZERO Hebrew bytes in this task. Any Hebrew in scope is\\n100|    either (a) pre-existing text left byte-identical, or (b) runtime data already sitting in a\\n101|    .json file, read and passed through — never typed, retyped, reformatted, or invented from\\n102|    memory. If the spec below doesn't hand you Hebrew text verbatim to copy, you don't write any.\\n103|\\n104|    ⚠️ EXECUTION SCOPE: run the Test Command below VERBATIM, character for character, exactly\\n105|