t time the bot did something you were glad about.\\n29|   - If you cancelled tomorrow, what is the FIRST thing you'd notice was gone.\\n30|   - What would you have to go back to doing yourself.\\n31|   - What would make you never cancel.\\n32|   Each core question gets one gentle follow-up probe (\\\"why\\\", \\\"tell me more about that moment\\\").\\n33|3. **Closing** (1–2 sentences) — thank, and one open \\\"anything I didn't ask about\\\" catch-all.\\n34|4. Add a one-line English facilitation note under each question (in [brackets]) telling Eitan what\\n35|   the question is really listening for — the English notes are for the interviewer, not read aloud.\\n36|\\n37|### Constraints:\\n38|- Hebrew body: singular male, 12–15 words/sentence, native Sabra spoken register.\\n39|- No jargon, no \\\"churn/retention/value proposition\\\" language leaking into the owner-facing Hebrew.\\n40|- The interviewer notes are English and clearly bracketed so they are never spoken.\\n41|\\n42|### Technical Details:\\n43|- Files to Create: `docs/research/site-bot/008_retention-interview-script.md`\\n44|- Files to Modify: NONE\\n45|- Files to Read: none required\\n46|- Dependencies: none (independent)\\n47|\\n48|## Acceptance Criteria\\n49|- [ ] File exists at the named path.\\n50|- [ ] Exactly five core questions, each with a follow-up probe and a bracketed English note.\\n51|- [ ] Hebrew reads as native Sabra spoken speech, singular male, sentences 12–15 words.\\n52|- [ ] Opening and closing present.\\n53|\\n54|## Implementation Notes\\n55|### Do:\\n56|- Write for the ear — this is spoken aloud on a phone call. Short, warm, conversational.\\n57|- Make Q3 and Q4 (the loss-aversion core) especially concrete and story-seeking.\\n58|### Don't:\\n59|- No Likert scales, no multiple choice — this is qualitative discovery.\\n60|\\n61|## Human Gate\\n62|This founder-facing Hebrew passes Eitan's spot-check before use (per AGENTS.md §3). Grammatical\\n63|correctness is not voice approval. Del